{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-24T22:26:09.018Z","data":{"text":"Task 7 complete.\n\n**Summary**\n\nI implemented `osq show` next step and verification history:\n\n- `src/core/status/show.ts`\n  - `SpecDetails` gains optional `next?: NextStep` and `verification?: VerificationHistory` (with `VerificationCheckRow`/`VerificationOutcomeRow` types).\n  - `getSpecDetails` attaches `readNextStep` for active and archived folders and omits it for rejected ones; for archived folders that require verification it also projects `check_ran`/`verification_recorded` rows from the change-level timeline.\n  - `formatSpecDetails` prints `Next: <formatNextStep>` right after `Status:`, then the `Verification:` section.\n- `tests/show-next-step.test.ts`: six new tests covering an archived `passed` change, a failed outcome, a `check_ran` row (and command shifting from `osq check` to `osq verified`), an active unplanned change, a rejected change with no `next`, and `--json` carrying `next`.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/show-next-step.test.ts`: 6/6 pass, exit 0.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: typecheck:cli, typecheck:ui, build, full test suite, and lint all completed (lint ran last, `biome check` clean over 493 files).\n\n**Notes for reviewer** (in the result file): `next`/`verification` are attached in `getSpecDetails` only, so web inspection via `getSpecDetailsFromFolder` is unaffected; the `Verification:` section byte format was unspecified, so I chose a labeled one-line-per-event format carrying every named field.\n\n`Touched: src/core/status/show.ts, tests/show-next-step.test.ts`"}}
